From: ma-abc123 <abc12302019@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 22:32:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] runtimes/feature: fix ill-formed const rvalue-ref move ctor

FeatureArray's move constructor was declared 'const FeatureArray&&'
while its body assigns other.p_ = nullptr. No standard-conforming
compiler accepts this (GCC 14 rejects the build outright). Drop the
stray const so the move constructor can actually take ownership.
---
 src/utils/feature_utils.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/utils/feature_utils.h b/src/utils/feature_utils.h
index 8b9456b..c578fd7 100644
--- a/src/utils/feature_utils.h
+++ b/src/utils/feature_utils.h
@@ -209,7 +209,7 @@ public:
         p_ = FeatureInstanceDupValue(other.p_);
     }
 
-    FeatureArray(const FeatureArray&& other)
+    FeatureArray(FeatureArray&& other)
     {
         p_ = other.p_;
         other.p_ = nullptr;
-- 
2.34.1

